sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-mirabet-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Hamant et al. (2008) & Heisler et al. (2010) pressurized SAM shell stress tensor, cortical microtubule alignment, PIN1-auxin phyllotactic mechanics, and (Pass 3) 3D multi-layered L1/L2/L3 Voronoi cell mesh with dynamic division planes — MorphoEval overall 86.9/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) evaluation of `2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py` (overall weighted score 86.9/100, DOWN from 92.6 in v2). The single v2 remediation item was addressed in reduced form: a 526-cell four-sheet L1/L2/L3a/L3b 3D Voronoi cell-centre mesh with wall springs, turgor on the exterior L1 faces, Jacobi-relaxed quasi-statics (relative residual 0.145), Lockhart creep and 181 volume-doubling divisions with dynamic anticlinal (Louveaux 2016 tension rule / Besson-Dumais 2011 Gibbs rule) and corpus (3D Gibbs) planes; the mesh L1 virial tension field now drives the 168-cell Auxin-PIN1-CMT ODE. The mesh reproduces the flank circumferential e_1 direction (81 % hoop-aligned) and the Lean Law 4 L1 load share (0.7144 vs 0.7143 across a 1-10x stiffness sweep), but NOT the radial growth of the membrane-law anisotropy magnitude (r = -0.11, RMSE 0.072), and the tension division rule yields only 38 % shortest-plane divisions vs 65-77 % measured (p = 5e-18); daughter symmetry 0.98 vs 0.81. The Pass 2 headline matches were found to be imposed: PIN1-CMT co-alignment 0.8491 via a 15.5 % switching-cell jitter model, post-ablation fraction 0.9103 via a fitted asymptote 0.918, compression S_CMT via a 1.48 factor, and the 50 um dome radius via calibration identity. 18 measurements (9 Pass 2 with caveats + 9 Pass 3), 13/13 self-test checks, 5 Lean theorems (0 sorrys), 9 DOI-verified references, SHA-256-pinned dataset (re-pinned). Overall 86.9/100 (faithfulness 84.3, reproducibility 92.9); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 94, Code-to-model traceability 90, Reproducibility package 94. Output judged: docs/media/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics_comparison.png: rendered output of 2008-hamant-meristem-microtubule-stress.py at d58a084, image/png, 1472695 B, 2520×2324 px, artifact_sha256 c36d8725eaa507fe05e4763c5e0e521e0b417c0c4ac585a68e02d6ebdf649328 (sha256 c36d8725eaa507fe05e4763c5e0e521e0b417c0c4ac585a68e02d6ebdf649328), spec_fingerprint bc94b13a6b26f42aa1073ace658e06dfd3f2592d5212c5761812f7f46fad2b02. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: bc94b13a6b26f42aa1073ace658e06dfd3f2592d5212c5761812f7f46fad2b02; artifact_sha256: c36d8725eaa507fe05e4763c5e0e521e0b417c0c4ac585a68e02d6ebdf649328; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics/arabidopsis_sam_meristem_specimen.jpg=3a8b54b71f7c780c..., datasets/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics_reference.json=d412b9c3432a07ad..., datasets/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics/paper_citations.bib=5abefe46e9337a7e..., datasets/auxin_pin1_meristem_mechanics/scout_manifest.json=1c17f6d448f3c423...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-auxin-pin1-meristem-mechanics-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hamant et al. (2008) Science 322:1650-1655 pressurized shell principal tensile stress tensor across spherical dome (sigma_theta = sigma_m = PR/2t), cylindrical flank (sigma_theta = 2*sigma_z = PR/t), and negative-Gaussian-curvature primordium boundary saddle crease, driving cortical microtubule (CMT) alignment and anisotropic Lockhart wall yielding | Heisler et al. (2010) PLoS Biol 8:e1000516 co-alignment between PIN1 auxin efflux carrier polarity and CMT orientation across L1 meristem cells (84.5% within +-30 deg) and synchronous circumferential reorientation following single-cell laser ablation | Louveaux et al. (2016) PNAS 113:E4294 shoot-apex division planes follow maximal tensile stress; 65-77% of planes are the shortest plane and 81% of divisions are symmetric (smaller daughter 40-50%); Reddy et al. (2004) L1/L2 divide anticlinally, corpus periclinally and anticlinally; reconstructed_in_script: Doubly-curved thin-shell Laplace-Young principal stress solver across all 4 SAM curvature zones + Fokker-Planck CMT nematic order S_CMT(A_sigma) + transverse-isotropic Lockhart cell-wall yielding | 168-cell paraboloidal L1 dome coupled Auxin-PIN1-CMT ODE simulator with the L1 stress field supplied by the 3D mesh (Pass 3) or by the Pass 2 analytic field (ablation); antisymmetric active flux conservation; 137.06 deg golden-angle phyllotaxis | Pass 3: 526-cell four-sheet L1/L2/L3a/L3b 3D Voronoi cell-centre mesh with wall springs, turgor on exterior faces, Jacobi-relaxed quasi-statics, per-cell virial tension tensor, Lockhart creep, division at volume doubling with Louveaux-2016 tension or Besson-Dumais-2011 Gibbs anticlinal planes (L1/L2) and 3D Gibbs planes (L3); L1 load share vs Lean Law 4; stiffness-ratio sweep | Kirsch circular laser-ablation wound stress redistribution (rim hoop stress doubling), lateral micro-vise compression, and 20 ug/mL oryzalin negative control; the post-ablation circumferential fraction is a fitted exponential relaxation, not a simulated reorientation | Automated segmentation of the Toluidine-Blue Arabidopsis SAM histological section (539 tunica-corpus nuclei, L1 dome contour & saddle crease) and apex-registered comparison of the mesh outer-L1 profile with the calibrated specimen contour; transfer_boundary: Axisymmetric/saddle thin-shell stress laws, 168-cell paraboloidal L1 dome and the 3D paraboloidal cell-centre mesh mapped to a single longitudinal histological SAM section; division-plane statistics compared with literature values (Louveaux 2016, Reddy 2004), not with the specimen; does_not_claim: A finite-element or vertex-model mechanical solution: the 3D mesh has cell-centre degrees of freedom only, no wall bending, no cell-volume constraint, stress-free insertion of new contacts, and does not reproduce the radial growth of the thin-shell anisotropy magnitude | That the 84.9% PIN1-CMT co-alignment, the 0.91 post-ablation circumferential fraction, the lateral-compression S_CMT or the 50 um calibrated dome radius are emergent model predictions (they are imposed by hard-coded noise/fit/fudge/calibration constants, see remediation)." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add an independent 3D specimen: a segmented confocal SAM stack (e.g. Louveaux 2016 / Reddy 2004 lineage data) to validate layer thicknesses, off-apex L1 profile (currently 5.5 um RMS, `compare_mesh_profile_with_specimen` L1443-L1467) and division-plane statistics against the specimen rather than literature means; replace the dome-radius calibration identity (`segment_arabidopsis_sam_specimen` L1389) by a scale bar.",
            "remediation needed: Close the division-plane gap: the Louveaux-2016 tension rule yields 38 % shortest-plane divisions vs 65-77 % measured (binomial p = 5e-18) and 98 % symmetric vs 81 % (`_choose_anticlinal_division_plane` L418-L487; measurements L2012-L2027) — implement the combined stress + geometry rule with realistic (non-Voronoi-regular) cell shapes and daughter-volume noise, and fix the 1.29 daughter/mother volume ratio from re-tessellation.",
            "remediation needed: Make the thin-shell anisotropy magnitude emergent: the mesh L1 bin-mean A_sigma does not grow with r as (1-q)/(3-q) (Pearson r = -0.11, RMSE 0.072, apex artefact 0.059; `simulate_multilayer_sam_mesh` L740-L800, measurements L1988-L2003) — add anisotropic L1 wall stiffness / a proper membrane limit (thin sheet, many cells per curvature radius) and remove the sunflower-lattice apex bias.",
            "remediation needed: Remove the imposed PIN1 angular noise model (`simulate_cellular_sam_pin1_cmt` L1163-L1166: N(0, 0.165) jitter plus 15.5 % switching cells) so that the PIN1-CMT co-alignment statistic emerges from the PIN1 allocation ODE; likewise replace the fitted post-ablation relaxation curve (asymptote 0.918, `simulate_mechanical_perturbations` L1271-L1273) by an actual ODE run on the Kirsch field and drop the 1.48 compression factor (L1281).",
            "remediation needed: Replace the cell-centre Voronoi mesh by a true vertex / finite-element model with vertex degrees of freedom, per-wall elastic anisotropy, wall bending and a cell-volume constraint, and insert new walls carrying their equilibrium tension (currently stress-free, `simulate_multilayer_sam_mesh` L653); the residual of the v2 item 'L1/L2/L3 polyhedral finite-element vertex mesh' is still open." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.869"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Autonomous Loop Slot 033 Pass 3 Assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .
}

